Q: How to avoid iterator invalidation in loop A: <p>The code does not utilize iterators. You should use them and a next iterator.</p>
<pre><code>for (auto it = m_bufs.begin(); it != m_bufs.end(); ;) {
    auto *cur = *it++;
    cur-&gt;doEffect(pDef, param);
}
</code></pre>
<p>This specific code in the Q can be made a bit shorter</p>
<pre><code>for (auto it = m_bufs.begin(); it != m_bufs.end(); ;) {
    (it++)-&gt;doEffect(pDef, param);
}
</code></pre>

Q: When INSERTing multiple rows into a database table, how to capture the first and last inserted id of the batch with CodeIgniter A: <p>Don't make it the responsibility of the model to do something nuanced like this. Write a very standard looking model method which simply inserts and unconditionally returns the id.</p>
<p>Let your controller (or a library if you want to keep your controller super skinny) perform the process of capturing the first and last inserted ids.</p>
<p>Model:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function storeReachout(array $reachoutInfo): int
{
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;insert('tbl_youtube', $reachoutInfo);
    return $this-&gt;db-&gt;insert_id();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function batchInsertReachout()
{
    $newRows = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('batch_of_rows') ?? [];

    $firstRowId = null;
    $lastRowId = null;
    foreach ($newRows as $row) {
        // overwrite previous on each iteration
        $lastRowId = $this-&gt;Youtube_model-&gt;storeReachout($row);

        // only store the first iteration
        $firstRowId ??= $lastRowId;
    }
    // do something with $firstRowId and $lastRowId
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to make VSCode format Django templates properly? A: <p>As you will most likely be using vscode workspace settings,
add extensions <strong>astral ruff</strong> and <strong>djlint</strong> then go to</p>
<blockquote>
<p>settings.json</p>
</blockquote>
<p>and add,</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
    &quot;editor.defaultFormatter&quot;: &quot;charliermarsh.ruff&quot;,
    &quot;editor.formatOnSave&quot;: true,
    &quot;[django-html]&quot;: {
        &quot;editor.defaultFormatter&quot;: &quot;monosans.djlint&quot;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now this will correctly format on every <strong>CMD+S</strong> or <strong>Ctrl+S</strong></p>
